# PyCharm's uv integration writes this; the project is pip-managed
# (requirements.txt + the --no-deps markdown2dash step a lockfile can't express)
uv.lock

# Visitor analytics data (regenerated at runtime)
visitor_analytics.json

# satellite reporter flock lease (lib/satellite_reporter.py)
.satellite_report.lease
visitor_analytics.json.lock

# Session working documents are LOCAL BY CONVENTION, network-wide: sync
# reports, handoffs, and kickoff briefs name hosts, topology, and process.
# Two public fleet repos were caught tracking theirs and clerkhook's staged
# handoff (naming the full satellite inventory) was one push from public
# (2026-08-24). The ignore rule is the enforcement, here and in every fork.
# X402-SYNC-REPORT.md lived in .git/info/exclude until the kit round — a
# per-clone exclude protects one checkout and no fork.
X402-SYNC-REPORT.md
HANDOFF-*.md
KICKOFF-*.md

# The .claude/ development kit IS shipped — it is how every fork inherits
# the network's behavioral contract, skills, and settings (the F1 fabric
# build, 2026-08-24). Everything else in .claude/ stays local: session
# scratch, screenshots (this repo has two), settings.local.json (per-seat
# model overrides), vendored iteration copies. Allow-list, not blanket
# ignore — a dir-level ignore cannot be re-included beneath, hence the /*
# form.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/

# Flask-Session server-side session store — created at runtime whenever
# Clerk is configured (lib/auth.py). Never source.
flask_session/
